1. A rotary cutting apparatus (10) comprising:  

a frame (12);  

at least one rotary device, preferably a first rotary device (14) and a second rotary device (16), supported by the frame (12) and configured to rotate about respective rotational axes (A, B);  

the first rotary device (14) including a first drum (37) and the second rotary device (16) including a second drum (38), each drum being configured to carry or support cutting elements for engagement with material to be cut; and  

a monitoring unit (28) embedded in at least one of the drums (37, 38),  

wherein the monitoring unit (28) is configured to measure working parameter data associated with operation of the rotary cutting apparatus (10) and to transmit the working parameter data to a receiver or control unit.

A rotary cutting apparatus comprising:

a frame;

first and second rotatable cutting assemblies supported by the frame, the first rotatable cutting assembly comprising a first shaft defining a first substantially horizontal rotational axis and a first drum mounted for rotation about the first substantially horizontal rotational axis, and the second rotatable cutting assembly comprising a second shaft defining a second substantially horizontal rotational axis and a second drum mounted for rotation about the second substantially horizontal rotational axis;

wherein the first and second substantially horizontal rotational axes are arranged substantially coplanar with one another;

at least one monitoring unit disposed within an interior of at least one of the first drum and the second drum, the at least one monitoring unit being configured to measure at least one working parameter associated with operation of the rotary cutting apparatus and to generate working-parameter information representative of the at least one measured working parameter; and

an interface transmission unit located externally of the at least one drum containing the at least one monitoring unit;

wherein the at least one monitoring unit is configured to transmit the working-parameter information to the interface transmission unit.

In some embodiments, the at least one working parameter comprises one or more of rotational speed, torque, vibration, temperature, angular position, acceleration, load, strain, pressure, operating time, wear condition, imbalance, or impact information associated with the at least one drum, shaft, or cutting assembly.

In some embodiments, the at least one monitoring unit comprises at least one sensor, a signal-processing circuit, and a wireless transmitter configured to transmit the working-parameter information from within the at least one drum to the external interface transmission unit.

In some embodiments, a respective monitoring unit is disposed within each of the first drum and the second drum, each respective monitoring unit being configured to transmit respective working-parameter information to the interface transmission unit.

In some embodiments, the interface transmission unit is configured to receive the working-parameter information and forward the working-parameter information to a controller, display, data logger, diagnostic system, or remote communication device.
